          "title": "You'll want to know: палатка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "палатка (palátka) — \"a tent\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Мы поставили палатку у реки. My postávili palátku u rekí. We put up the tent by the river."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Ставить палатку — to pitch a tent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "палатка (palátka) is usually traced to палата 'a chamber, a hall', which goes back through Greek to Latin palātium 'a palace' (Lewis & Short). EtymDB lists палатка (palátka) with the sense 'tent' but no source."
            }
          ]
        },
